      "content": "While Benadryl can help with general allergy symptoms, the combination of widespread hives and throat tightness suggests a potentially worsening allergic reaction. **If your throat remains tight, you experience difficulty breathing, swelling around your face or lips, or dizziness, seek emergency care immediately** as this could indicate anaphylaxis. If symptoms are milder but persistent despite over-the-counter medication, it is still wise to contact your doctor or visit an urgent care clinic for proper evaluation and guidance. Only use the extra dose of antihistamine if you are comfortable doing so, but monitor your respiratory status very closely.",
